      "message": "When `n_topright_px \u003c 0` or `n_bottomleft_px \u003c 0` (all Zone 2 modes `90 \u003c p_angle \u003c 180` and `filter_intra`), `above_row` and `left_col` are only initialized up to `num_top_pixels_needed` (`txwpx`) and `num_left_pixels_needed` (`txhpx`), leaving `above_row[txwpx .. txwpx + txhpx - 1]` and `left_col[txhpx .. txhpx + txwpx - 1]` uninitialized before the zeroed tail at `+ txwpx + txhpx`. SIMD kernels such as `av1_upsample_intra_edge_sse4_1` and `dr_prediction_z2_HxW_avx2` (`_mm_maskload_epi32` + `_mm_shuffle_epi8`) read across that uninitialized gap and taint `dst` under Clang MemorySanitizer (`-fsanitize\u003dmemory`). Please start the tail `memset` at `above_row + num_top_pixels_needed` and `left_col + num_left_pixels_needed` (gated on `need_above` / `need_left`), and apply the same fix in `highbd_build_directional_and_filter_intra_predictors` at lines 1487–1488 (where `highbd_dr_prediction_z2_*_neon` likewise over-reads `left_col[txhpx ..]`).",
